  "body": "Idea from the reporter (2026-11-23), after asking CamCraft's AI Chat to \"create a cube\" and program it. Today the chat has only CamCraft's own MCP tools. SolidCraft (the sister CAD app) has its own MCP server (parametric parts: sketches, extrudes, fillets, holes, measure, export STEP / .sc). CamCraft already imports `.sc` / `.solidcraft` designs.\n\nOpen questions (research before code):\n1. Connection: CamCraft's chat as an MCP client of a running SolidCraft (local stdio or HTTP), opt-in, with the user's approval per server. Alternatively, a shared agent outside both apps.\n2. Hand-off: SolidCraft exports, then CamCraft imports. Keep a link so a design change in SolidCraft re-imports and marks the operations stale (#2-level design: which features map to CAM features: holes, pockets).\n3. Safety and undo: each app keeps its own undo history; one \"Undo turn\" across two apps is hard. Decide what the chat may change in each.\n4. Permissions and privacy: which design data is sent to a cloud model.\n\nDone means: a research comment answers these questions, and concrete sub-issues are filed (AGENTS.md \"needs-research\").\n",
